# Template — install.sh substitutes __USER__ and installs the result to
# /etc/sudoers.d/groove-tracker-web (via visudo -c, which validates syntax
# before it's ever placed where sudo will read it).
#
# Grants the web UI's user exactly these systemctl invocations on
# groove-tracker.service and groove-tracker-web.service, and nothing else
# -- the web UI process itself still runs unprivileged (see
# groove-tracker-web.service), it just shells out to `sudo -n systemctl
# ...` for these specific commands. The restart of groove-tracker-web
# itself is what the dashboard's Update button uses to pick up new code
# after a git pull -- see webui/service_control.py's restart_self_delayed().
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /bin/systemctl start groove-tracker.service, /bin/systemctl stop groove-tracker.service, /bin/systemctl restart groove-tracker.service, /bin/systemctl restart groove-tracker-web.service
